hadiths[6]{hadithnumber,text}:
"95","Musa ibn Isma'il narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Qatadah: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Separate Sha'ban from Ramadan."
"96","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Mu'adh narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Qatadah, from Khalid - meaning Ibn Durayk - from Ibn Muhayriz, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to deem the pre-dawn meal desirable even if only sips of water."
"97","Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from al-Harith ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, from Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Thawban, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There are two dawns. As for the one that is like the tail of the wolf, it permits nothing and prohibits nothing. As for the spreading one that covers the horizon, it permits prayer and prohibits food."
"98","Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us, from Khalid, from Isma'il, from Hakim - meaning Ibn Jabir - he said: I was told that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was eating the pre-dawn meal when Bilal came to him and said: Prayer, O Messenger of Allah. He remained silent and gave him no reply. So Bilal returned and said: Prayer, O Messenger of Allah, morning has come upon you. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May Allah have mercy on Bilal; were it not for Bilal I would have hoped that concession would be granted to us until sunrise."
"99","Musaddad narrated to us, from Hushaym, from Husayn, from Mu'adh ibn Zuhrah, that it reached him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he broke his fast, would say: O Allah, for You I fasted, and upon Your provision I broke my fast."
"100","Qutaybah ibn Sa'id informed us, and Ibn Wahb - both said: Al-Layth narrated to us, from 'Uqayl, from Ibn Shihab, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no showing off in fasting."
